WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.296
You type an idea and click Save. It shows up in your list.

2
00:00:04.326 --> 00:00:07.497
It feels instant. Three things just happened.

3
00:00:07.927 --> 00:00:11.004
First, your browser sends the idea to your app.

4
00:00:11.034 --> 00:00:12.921
The app isn't on your laptop.

5
00:00:12.951 --> 00:00:15.631
It's running on a server, somewhere else.

6
00:00:16.061 --> 00:00:20.295
The app checks the request. Is there actually a title?

7
00:00:20.325 --> 00:00:24.716
Is it a sensible length? If not, it says no, right here.

8
00:00:25.146 --> 00:00:29.643
Second, the app writes one line of SQL and hands it to the database.

9
00:00:29.673 --> 00:00:30.775
Insert this idea.

10
00:00:31.205 --> 00:00:36.180
The database stores it as a new row in a table, and answers: done.

11
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:41.117
Third, the app sends the updated list back to your browser, and the page redraws.

12
00:00:41.547 --> 00:00:43.687
Browser. App. Database. And back.

13
00:00:43.717 --> 00:00:48.028
Almost everything you'll build is some version of that round trip.
